who took it the wrong way.

210
00:18:29,921 --> 00:18:32,382
So this whole time... you knew that?

211
00:18:34,634 --> 00:18:38,054
Uhh, let's just leave it at that! Now
that I'm saying it out loud it's totally

212
00:18:38,138 --> 00:18:41,558
- making me feel worse.
- Poor thing.

213
00:18:41,641 --> 00:18:44,978
Such a heartbreaker... Kazehaya...

214
00:18:45,103 --> 00:18:46,855
Th-That's why, I don't
really know how to say this but...

215
00:18:46,938 --> 00:18:48,064
You know...

216
00:18:49,274 --> 00:18:54,988
Maybe for now... it'd be best if you just
tried to keep your distance from him.

217
00:18:55,613 --> 00:18:58,074
- For both your sakes.
- Wait, wha...?!

218
00:18:58,158 --> 00:19:02,829
It'll be good! You'll be on your own, free
to enjoy school life however you please!

219
00:19:03,037 --> 00:19:07,750
Kazehaya too, he'll be
relieved that he's finished his job--

220
00:19:09,002 --> 00:19:12,630
Y'see Sadako... He has someone he likes.

221
00:19:16,968 --> 00:19:19,637
I was already flat out rejected, so...

222
00:19:25,268 --> 00:19:28,062
I wasn't planning on telling you, but...

223
00:19:28,146 --> 00:19:31,733
Don't you think it's kinda pointless to
be so wrapped up in him? Plus, you don't

224
00:19:31,816 --> 00:19:35,403
want to cause trouble
for him either, right?

225
00:19:35,486 --> 00:19:40,533
That's why. How do I put this... Think of
it like being reborn! You can find a new

226
00:19:40,617 --> 00:19:45,538
love somewhere else! There's a
lot of fun waiting to be had so...

227
00:19:46,456 --> 00:19:48,333
Huh? Hold on! Sadako?

228
00:19:50,668 --> 00:19:54,172
I see... so there really was... another girl.

229
00:19:57,884 --> 00:19:58,885
Come on...

